<body>
<div class="reading-track" aria-hidden="true"><div class="reading-progress" id="readingProgress"></div></div>
<div class="reading-label" id="readingLabel">0% read</div>

<header>
  <div>
    <div class="eyebrow">A Supernatural Horror Story</div>
    <h1>NISHAACHARUDU</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">The Demon Who Walks in Silence</p>
    <div class="episode">Episode 1 · The Silent Well</div>
  </div>
</header>

<main>
<article class="story" id="story">
  <p>The sun was slowly disappearing behind the mountains.</p>

  <p>Deep inside a dense forest, several police officers were searching through the bushes. A few police dogs were running ahead, sniffing the ground and following different paths.</p>

  <p>"Check that side!"</p>
  <p>"Don't leave any area unchecked!"</p>

  <p>The forest echoed with police whistles and desperate voices.</p>

  <p>A little boy had been missing for two days.</p>

  <p>His parents were also searching desperately.</p>

  <p class="shout">"RAJU! RAJU!"</p>

  <p>His mother screamed his name repeatedly.</p>

  <p>"Raju! Where are you, my son? Please answer me!"</p>

  <p>She pushed through the bushes, ignoring the scratches on her hands.</p>

  <p>But there was no response.</p>

  <p>After searching for hours, her strength finally gave up. She walked towards a large tree and sat beneath it.</p>

  <p>Her eyes were swollen from crying.</p>

  <p>"Please come back, my child. I won't scold you. I promise. Just come back to me..."</p>

  <p>She began crying uncontrollably.</p>

  <p>Her husband approached her slowly. He was equally exhausted, with tears running down his cheeks.</p>

  <p>He sat beside her.</p>

  <p>"Don't lose hope. We'll find him."</p>

  <p>She held his shirt tightly.</p>

  <p>"What if something happened to him? What if he's hungry? What if he's crying somewhere and nobody can hear him?"</p>

  <p>Her husband couldn't answer.</p>

  <p>He simply wrapped his arms around her and held her tightly.</p>

  <p>He was crying too.</p>

  <p>A police officer approached them.</p>

  <p>"Sir, it's getting dark. We have searched most of the forest, but we haven't found him. There are wild animals in this area. It's becoming dangerous to continue searching tonight."</p>

  <p>The father looked at him desperately.</p>

  <p>"Please, sir. Just one more hour. My son could be somewhere here."</p>

  <p>"I'm sorry. We will return tomorrow morning with more officers and search again. Please go home safely."</p>

  <p>The parents had no choice.</p>

  <p>They slowly walked towards their vehicle, looking back at the forest again and again.</p>

  <p>As darkness swallowed the forest, a distant roar echoed between the trees.</p>

  <p>Then another.</p>

  <p>And another.</p>

  <div class="divider"></div>
  <p class="time">11:47 PM · Deep inside the forest</p>

  <p>The forest was alive.</p>

  <p>Wolves howled in the distance.</p>

  <p>Wild boars moved through the bushes.</p>

  <p>Owls watched from the branches.</p>

  <p>Insects filled the darkness with their continuous sounds.</p>

  <p>Suddenly...</p>

  <p>A figure appeared between two enormous trees.</p>

  <p>It was walking slowly.</p>

  <p>There was something unusual about its movement.</p>

  <p>It didn't seem to be afraid of anything.</p>

  <p>A wolf standing nearby suddenly stopped.</p>

  <p>Its ears lowered.</p>

  <p>It turned around and ran.</p>

  <p>A group of wild boars disappeared into the bushes.</p>

  <p>Even the owls abandoned their branches.</p>

  <p>One by one, every animal moved away.</p>

  <p>Then...</p>

  <p class="shout">Silence.</p>

  <p class="shout">Absolute silence.</p>

  <p>Not a single cricket.</p>

  <p>Not a single insect.</p>

  <p>Not even the buzzing of a mosquito.</p>

  <p>The leaves stopped moving.</p>

  <p>The figure continued walking.</p>

  <p>It passed between the trees and approached an abandoned stone well.</p>

  <p>The well was extremely old. Moss covered its walls, and thick roots surrounded its entrance.</p>

  <p>The figure stopped.</p>

  <p>It was carrying something.</p>

  <p>A small body wrapped in a dirty cloth.</p>

  <p>It slowly lifted the body and dropped it into the well.</p>

  <p class="sound">THUD!</p>

  <p>The sound disappeared into the darkness below.</p>

  <p>The figure leaned forward.</p>

  <p>Then its face slowly stretched into an unusually wide smile.</p>

  <p>Deep inside the well...</p>

  <p>Five children were sitting together.</p>

  <p>They were terrified.</p>

  <p>Their clothes were dirty. Their faces were covered in tears. One little girl was holding another boy's hand tightly.</p>

  <p>They had been crying for hours.</p>

  <p>When they saw the figure looking down at them, their crying became louder.</p>

  <p>"Please... let us go!"</p>

  <p>"Please! I want my mother!"</p>

  <p>The figure raised one finger.</p>

  <p>It placed the finger against its lips.</p>

  <p>"Shhhhh..."</p>

  <p>Every child immediately stopped crying.</p>

  <p>Not because they wanted to.</p>

  <p>But because they were too frightened to make another sound.</p>

  <p>The figure continued smiling.</p>

  <p>Then it slowly disappeared into the darkness.</p>

  <div class="divider"></div>
  <p class="time">The next morning · Police station</p>

  <p>The police station was unusually busy.</p>

  <p>Officers were discussing the missing boy's case. Some were checking photographs, while others were preparing search teams.</p>

  <p>The station telephone kept ringing.</p>

  <p>Suddenly...</p>

  <p>A man and woman rushed through the entrance.</p>

  <p>"Sir! Please help us!"</p>

  <p>Both were crying.</p>

  <p>An officer stood up.</p>

  <p>"What happened?"</p>

  <p>"Our child... our child is missing!"</p>

  <p>The woman could barely speak.</p>

  <p>"He was sleeping at home last night. When we woke up this morning, he wasn't there. We searched everywhere. We checked our neighbours' houses. We even searched the nearby roads."</p>

  <p>The father placed his son's photograph on the officer's desk.</p>

  <p>"Please, sir. Find him. He's only seven years old."</p>

  <p>The officer carefully collected the information.</p>

  <p>"When did you last see him?"</p>

  <p>"Last night, around 9 PM. He was sleeping beside us."</p>

  <p>"Did anyone enter your house?"</p>

  <p>"We don't know, sir. We didn't hear anything."</p>

  <p>The woman started crying again.</p>

  <p>"Please bring my child back. I'll do anything. Please!"</p>

  <p>The officer assured them that the police would investigate.</p>

  <p>After registering the complaint, the parents returned home.</p>

  <p>A few minutes later, an officer walked towards the missing-person notice board.</p>

  <p>There were already five photographs.</p>

  <p>He placed the new photograph beside them.</p>

  <p>Six children.</p>

  <p>Six innocent faces.</p>

  <p>Six missing lives.</p>

  <p>Underneath the photographs, someone had written:</p>

  <p class="shout">MISSING – INFORMATION REQUESTED</p>

  <p>A senior officer entered the room.</p>

  <p>"What is happening here? Why are the missing-child cases increasing?"</p>

  <p>The inspector stood up.</p>

  <p>"Sir, we now have six missing children from the surrounding areas. We have searched the forest, nearby villages and roads. But there are no proper clues."</p>

  <p>"Six children? In such a short period?"</p>

  <p>"Yes, sir."</p>

  <p>The senior officer stared at the photographs.</p>

  <p>"Listen carefully. I want updates every hour. Coordinate with every nearby police station. Get additional forces if necessary. We cannot allow another child to disappear."</p>

  <p>The inspector nodded.</p>

  <p>But neither of them noticed something strange.</p>

  <p>All six children had disappeared during the night.</p>

  <p>And none of their families had heard anything.</p>

  <div class="divider"></div>
  <p class="time">Somewhere deep inside the forest</p>

  <p>A strange sound emerged from beneath the ground.</p>

  <p>A small crack appeared in the dry earth.</p>

  <p>Then another.</p>

  <p>An old hand slowly emerged from the soil.</p>

  <p>A man opened his eyes.</p>

  <p>His body was covered with ash. His long hair was tangled, and several strange symbols were painted across his chest.</p>

  <p>He was an Agora.</p>

  <p>He slowly stood up.</p>

  <p>For a few moments, he stared at the sky.</p>

  <p>Then his expression changed.</p>

  <p>Anger filled his eyes.</p>

  <p>He picked up a wooden staff and began walking towards the village.</p>

  <p>As he walked, he started chanting unfamiliar spells.</p>

  <p>His voice grew louder.</p>

  <p>Suddenly, he stopped and screamed:</p>

  <p class="shout">"DEMONS ARE WALKING AMONG US!"</p>

  <p>His voice echoed through the forest.</p>

  <p>"NO ONE WILL BE SAVED!"</p>

  <p>He continued towards the village.</p>

  <p>"KEEP YOUR CHILDREN CLOSE! DO NOT LET THEM OUT OF YOUR SIGHT!"</p>

  <p>Villagers working near the fields heard the screams.</p>

  <p>Some ran towards their houses.</p>

  <p>Others stood frozen.</p>

  <p>The Agora entered the village.</p>

  <p>He walked directly into the centre and sat beneath an ancient banyan tree.</p>

  <p>Villagers gathered around him.</p>

  <p>One elderly man approached.</p>

  <p>"Swami, what happened? Why are you saying these things?"</p>

  <p>The Agora looked directly into his eyes.</p>

  <p>"Something has entered this land. Something that should never have awakened."</p>

  <p>"Who is it, Swami?"</p>

  <p>The Agora slammed his staff against the ground.</p>

  <p>"Don't ask its name!"</p>

  <p>Everyone became silent.</p>

  <p>He took out a small container filled with a dark liquid.</p>

  <p>He began performing a ritual.</p>

  <p>He poured the liquid in front of every house.</p>

  <p>He walked around the village, marking its boundaries with the same substance.</p>

  <p>He chanted continuously.</p>

  <p>Finally, he returned to the banyan tree.</p>

  <p>He looked at everyone.</p>

  <p>"Listen carefully. Nobody leaves this village after sunset. Lock your doors. Keep your children beside you. And whatever you hear tonight..."</p>

  <p>He paused.</p>

  <p>"...DO NOT OPEN YOUR DOORS."</p>

  <p>A woman asked nervously:</p>

  <p>"What will happen if we open them?"</p>

  <p>The Agora slowly turned towards her.</p>

  <p>His eyes widened.</p>

  <p>"Then it will know that someone is inside."</p>

  <div class="divider"></div>
  <p class="time">Same night · Abandoned well</p>

  <p>The forest was silent again.</p>

  <p>The mysterious figure approached the old well.</p>

  <p>This time, its movements were faster.</p>

  <p>Something had changed.</p>

  <p>It stopped near the entrance.</p>

  <p>Below, the children were sitting together.</p>

  <p>One little boy whispered:</p>

  <p>"Will someone come to save us?"</p>

  <p>Another child started crying.</p>

  <p>"I want my mother..."</p>

  <p>Suddenly, a shadow covered the opening.</p>

  <p>The figure was back.</p>

  <p>It slowly looked down.</p>

  <p>But this time, it wasn't smiling.</p>

  <p>Its face showed anger.</p>

  <p>It looked towards the village.</p>

  <p>The Agora's ritual had disturbed something.</p>

  <p>The children noticed the change in its expression.</p>

  <p>One girl slowly moved backwards.</p>

  <p>The youngest boy began trembling.</p>

  <p>Then...</p>

  <p>The figure placed its hand against the stone wall.</p>

  <p>A deep, terrifying sound emerged from somewhere beneath the well.</p>

  <p class="sound">KRRRRRRRR...</p>

  <p>The children covered their ears.</p>

  <p>The figure leaned closer.</p>

  <p>Its mouth slowly opened into a horrifying smile.</p>

  <p>And then...</p>

  <p>It whispered something.</p>

  <p>Something none of the children had ever heard before.</p>

  <p>The youngest boy began screaming.</p>

  <p>The others followed.</p>

  <p>Their cries echoed through the well and disappeared into the darkness.</p>

  <p>Above them, the figure remained completely still.</p>

  <p>Watching.</p>

  <p>Waiting.</p>

  <div class="ending">
    <strong>END OF EPISODE 1</strong>
    <span>THE SILENT WELL</span>
  </div>
</article>
</main>

<footer>Created by <strong>Vijay Krishna</strong></footer>

<script>
  const progress = document.getElementById('readingProgress');
  const label = document.getElementById('readingLabel');

  function updateReadingProgress() {
    const scrollable = document.documentElement.scrollHeight - window.innerHeight;
    const percent = scrollable > 0 ? Math.min(100, Math.max(0, (window.scrollY / scrollable) * 100)) : 100;
    progress.style.width = percent + '%';
    label.textContent = Math.round(percent) + '% read';
  }

  window.addEventListener('scroll', updateReadingProgress, { passive: true });
  window.addEventListener('resize', updateReadingProgress);
  updateReadingProgress();
</script>
</body>
